# Wi-Fi test builds (`WIFI=1 ./build.sh kernel`, docs/wifi.md), on top of
# vt10101.config, which since 2026-10-28 carries what our dongle
# needs (cfg80211, mac80211, rtl8xxxu, the zstd firmware loader, the fixed
# regulator for VBUS). This adds the spare drivers, for a dongle that isn't
# the TL-WN821N's RTL8192CU: ath9k_htc (the AR7010 its "v4.2" label
# promised, and the AR9271), MT7601U and RT5370/RT3070 (rt2800usb), what
# cheap 2.4 GHz dongles carry. The initramfs side of WIFI=1 (wpa_supplicant,
# iw, firmware) is build/wifi-userland.py.
#
# Built in, not modules, like everything else here. The dongle shows up long
# after the initramfs is mounted (the role switch to host comes from
# userspace), so the drivers' request_firmware finds /lib/firmware.
CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_ATH=y
CONFIG_ATH9K_HTC=y
CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_MEDIATEK=y
CONFIG_MT7601U=y
CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_RALINK=y
CONFIG_RT2X00=y
CONFIG_RT2800USB=y
CONFIG_RT2800USB_RT53XX=y
CONFIG_RT2800USB_RT55XX=y
